---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Follow opaque product-issued passive continuations; closing the view only stops observation

Usage: pse observe follow [OPTIONS] --reader <READER> --request <REQUEST>

Options:
  -C <checkout>
      --reader <READER>
      --format <FORMAT>            Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --request <REQUEST>          Initial product follow request; resume coordinates remain product-owned
      --fields <FIELDS>            Select comma-separated payload fields while retaining identity, state and coverage
      --samples <SAMPLES>          Maximum whole snapshots emitted before observation stops [default: 32]
      --budget <BUDGET>            Limit payload array records; retain complete evidence as an artifact
      --interval-ms <INTERVAL_MS>  Minimum polling interval; native progress never awaits this renderer [default: 1000]
      --timeout <TIMEOUT>          Observer allowance; its expiry does not time out the original workload [default: 30]
  -h, --help                       Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Follow opaque product-issued passive continuations; closing the view only stops observation

Usage: pse observe follow [OPTIONS] --reader <READER> --request <REQUEST>

Options:
  -C <checkout>


      --reader <READER>


      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --request <REQUEST>
          Initial product follow request; resume coordinates remain product-owned

      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated payload fields while retaining identity, state and coverage

      --samples <SAMPLES>
          Maximum whole snapshots emitted before observation stops

          [default: 32]

      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit payload array records; retain complete evidence as an artifact

      --interval-ms <INTERVAL_MS>
          Minimum polling interval; native progress never awaits this renderer

          [default: 1000]

      --timeout <TIMEOUT>
          Observer allowance; its expiry does not time out the original workload

          [default: 30]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
